{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far points to config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 acc as the current best, with multiprofile contributing the largest single gain (+0.092 over singleprofile) and avgpool outperforming transformer (+0.04). However, the fusion strategy has only been tested as 'concat' across all multimodal runs. config_019 is the minimal controlled change from the best config—swapping concat for weighted fusion while holding every other factor constant. This directly tests whether the modality combination strategy can be further optimized, which is a high-leverage design choice given that the image modality alone is very weak (0.208) and the multimodal gain over RNA-only is modest (+0.042 in singleprofile). If weighted fusion helps, it is a free improvement; if not, it confirms concat is sufficient and we can redirect budget toward image encoder or RNA encoder upgrades. Under a limited budget, this single-variable test from the best-known configuration is the most information-efficient next step."
}

